    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Joyabuy:</strong> Average purchase speed of <strong>6 to 12 hours</strong>. While reliable, their manual ordering queue can experience bottlenecks during peak weekend drops.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>CNFans:</strong> Average purchase speed of <strong>12 to 24+ hours</strong>. Due to their massive user base, CNFans occasionally suffers from backlog delays, meaning high-demand spreadsheet items might sell out before order execution.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Warehouse Processing & QC Turnaround</h2>
  <p>
    Once your items arrive at the agent's warehouse, staff must inspect, weigh, and photograph them. Having fast access to quality control (QC) photos is vital so you can trigger domestic returns if defects are present.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Kakobuy</strong> stands out in 2026 due to its newly launched **4K High-Definition QC Video** options, delivering sharp visual checks within 12 hours of package check-in. <strong>CNFans</strong> offers solid, multi-angle static photos, but their intake delays during holiday rushes can stall check-ins for up to 3 days. <strong>Joyabuy</strong> maintains a stable, average 24-hour turnaround with high-resolution imagery.
  </p>

